@page
@inject Microsoft.AspNetCore.Antiforgery.IAntiforgery Antiforgery
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>   
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.6;                     
            color: #333;
        }

        h1, h2 {
            color: #1a1a1a;
        }

        h1 {
            border-bottom: 2px solid #ccc;
            padding-bottom: 10px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong>1/1/2025</p>

    <p><strong>SortieLog.com</strong> (“we”, “our”, or “us”) is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your personal information when you use our services.</p>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>When you sign in using your <strong>Google or Microsoft account</strong>, we collect only the necessary information to identify and authenticate you. This may include:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Your name</li>
        <li>Your email address</li>
        <li>Your unique user ID provided by the authentication provider</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> collect or access your password or any unrelated data from your Google or Microsoft account.</p>

    <h2>2. Purpose of Data Collection</h2>
    <p>Our site helps <strong>pilots retrieve and review tracks of flights they’ve flown</strong>, including weather conditions at the time and location of each flight. We also provide a private, digital logbook feature.</p>
    <p>To provide this service, we may collect and store:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Flight path data (e.g., GPS positions and timestamps)</li>
        <li>Weather data at the time and location of the flight</li>
        <li>FAA pilot information (used to create a unique logbook)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>All data is securely stored in a <strong>Microsoft SQL Server</strong> database.</p>

    <h2>3. Data Use and Storage</h2>
    <p>We use your information only to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Authenticate your identity</li>
        <li>Retrieve and present your flight and weather information</li>
        <li>Save your flight data to your personal logbook</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Your data is <strong>never shared, sold, or disclosed</strong> to any third parties.</p>

    <h2>4. Data Security</h2>
    <p>We follow <strong>industry best practices</strong> to protect your personal and flight data from unauthorized access. This includes:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Secure authentication methods</li>
        <li>Encrypted communications (HTTPS)</li>
        <li>Role-based access controls</li>
        <li>Regular updates and security audits</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
    <p>You have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Access your personal data</li>
        <li>Request deletion of your data or logbook</li>
        <li>Withdraw authorization to use Google or Microsoft authentication</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To exercise your rights, contact us at <strong>privacy@sortielog.com</strong>.</p>

    <h2>6. Children’s Privacy</h2>
    <p>This service is intended for licensed pilots and is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from children.</p>

    <h2>7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy periodically. If significant changes occur, we will notify users through the website or email.</p>

    <h2>8. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>If you have any questions or concerns about this policy or your data, contact us at:</p>
    <p>
        <strong>Email:</strong>privacy@sortielog.com<br>
        <strong>Website:</strong>https://www.sortielog.com
    </p>
    </body>
</html>
